      "message": "The reason I split `process_l` in another block was because is annotated with `REQUIRES(mThreadMutex)`, and clang doesn\u0027t support the thread safe annotation with std::unique_lock (I think).\n\nI can remove the thread annotation and have something like this, but I think removing the annotation is also not ideal because it causes confusion on whether of not the processing should hold the lock.\n```\n    while (true) {\n        std::unique_lock l(mThreadMutex);\n        if (mExit) {\n            LOG(WARNING) \u003c\u003c __func__ \u003c\u003c \" EXIT!\";\n            return;\n        }\n        process_l();\n    }\n```\n\nmExit and mStop does not need to under condition variable for the second block because here we only need to make sure get the latest value before process.\n\nI should write more context about the sequence in commit message, but basically it was happening when a stopThread() was called right after `mCv.wait` and before `process()`, in this case vts think the processing thread has been stopped but it\u0027s actually producing data, which cause the test case fail.",
